  "notes": [
    "PREFER `expr` strings ('$actor.gold >= 100 && $actor.alive') for any guard (precondition, effect.condition, termination). Single grammar, fewer pitfalls.",
    "Built-in effect operations and EVERY registered custom op live in `live_capabilities.effect_operations` \u2014 there is no hidden vocabulary.",
    "Use role='agent' only for decision-making participants, with matching actions. Autonomous systems use role='object' and executable derived rules, triggers, physics or domain modules; they do not need dummy decision agents.",
    "termination_conditions are optional but recommended; without one the game only stops at engine.max_rounds.",
    "Domain modules (chess, monopoly, prediction_market, \u2026) are referenced by name \u2014 DO NOT emit Python. Pick from `live_capabilities.domain_modules`.",
    "Visualization is the ONLY thing an env-builder agent generates as code \u2014 and even that is sandboxed Konva. Game logic is always declarative JSON."
  ],
